// Two spans, so this also checks that inputs are scheduled by tick rather than
// merely applied.
//
// Reversal first brakes the 9m/s eastward motion, then accelerates west.
// Summing the bounded motor steps (each tick's change ramped over four
// substeps) leaves x=1.30465173 after 60 ticks.
// Facing has to travel from +PI/2 to -PI/2, an arc of PI radians; at 14 rad/s
// that takes 13.5 ticks, so 30 is comfortably enough to arrive.
//
// The seam is the point: a turn that took the long way round would still end at
// -PI/2 and pass this. What it would not survive is `the_short_way_round_the_seam_is_short`
// in sim's own tests — the two are complementary, which is why both exist.
(
    description: "Reversing direction brakes carried momentum and ends up facing the new way.",
    setup: (),
    inputs: [
        (at: 0,  ticks: 30, dir: (1.0, 0.0)),
        (at: 30, ticks: 30, dir: (-1.0, 0.0)),
    ],
    budget: (ticks: 60),
    expect: (
        player_pos: (x: 1.3046517, z: 0.0, tol: 0.001),
        facing: (value: -1.5708, tol: 0.0001),
    ),
)
